# Rules with several product patterns, one of which holds molecules that no
# bond joins.
#
# "." within a product pattern says its molecules end up in one complex, and
# "+" between product patterns says the molecules of different patterns end up
# in different complexes. Both apply to every molecule of the pattern, not only
# to the molecules at the bonds the rule deletes.
#
# KeepC deletes the A-B bond and writes "A.C + B", where C is joined to A.B
# only by "." in the reactant pattern. On a complex where C is bonded to A
# (CAB) it fires, and CAB falls to 0. Where C is bonded to B instead (ABC), C
# would stay with B and leave A: it must never fire, and ABC stays at 100.
#
# JoinEG deletes the three bonds of the chain E-F-G-H and writes "E.G + F + H".
# On the chain E and G come apart, so it must never fire: Chain stays at 100.
# On a ring where E and G are also bonded to each other it fires, and Ring
# falls to 0.
#
# Bridge deletes the P-Q bond and writes "P.X.R + Q", where X is a molecule it
# creates to join P to R. P and R are held together only through X. It fires
# on every P.Q, and PQ falls to 0.
#
# BioNetGen's network generator agrees. Given this model it produces three
# reactions, KeepC on CAB, JoinEG on the ring and Bridge.
#
# NFsim placed in the product patterns only the molecules at the bonds a rule
# deletes, and required "." only between the two molecules of a deleted bond,
# so KeepC and JoinEG fired on both of their complexes.

begin model
begin parameters
  k   1.0
  kb  1.0
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b,c)
  B(a,c)
  C(a,b)
  E(f,g)
  F(e,g)
  G(f,h,e)
  H(g)
  P(q,x)
  Q(p)
  R(x)
  X(p,r)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,c).C(a!2,b)                       100
  A(b!1,c).B(a!1,c!2).C(a,b!2)                       100
  E(f!1,g).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,h!3,e).H(g!3)           100
  E(f!1,g!4).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,h!3,e!4).H(g!3)       100
  P(q!1,x).Q(p!1)                                    100
  R(x)                                               100
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  CAB    A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,c).C(a!2,b)
  Molecules  ABC    A(b!1,c).B(a!1,c!2).C(a,b!2)
  Molecules  Chain  E(f!1,g).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,h!3,e).H(g!3)
  Molecules  Ring   E(f!1,g!4).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,h!3,e!4).H(g!3)
  Molecules  PQ     P(q!1).Q(p!1)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  KeepC:  A(b!1).B(a!1).C() -> A(b).C() + B(a)   k
  JoinEG: E(f!1).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,h!3).H(g!3) -> E(f).G(f,h) + F(e,g) + H(g)   k
  Bridge: P(q!1,x).Q(p!1) + R(x) -> P(q,x!2).X(p!2,r!3).R(x!3) + Q(p)   kb
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
